   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How it is formed",
     "texto": [
      "Future of **avere** or **essere** + participle: **avrò finito** (I will have finished), **sarò arrivato** (I will have arrived).",
      "With **essere** the participle agrees: **sarò arrivata** (I will have arrived, she)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When it is used",
     "texto": [
      "For a future action that happens before another: **Quando avrò finito, ti chiamerò** (when I have finished, I will call you). In conversation it is also common to use the present with future meaning: **Quando avrò finito, ti chiamo**. The future perfect also expresses a conjecture: **Sarà già partito** (he has probably already left)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
